Each hand is ranked into one of the standard poker categories, from high card up to straight flush. Ties within a category are settled by comparing the card values, starting with the biggest group of matching cards (for example, the pair before the single cards). An ace counts low in the A-2-3-4-5 straight, so that's a 5-high straight. Both "10" and "T" work as the ten."}
